--- ENV-02, ENV-05: count and empty agree ---
a number called 'the badge' is environment's count.
a boolean called 'the compass' is environment's empty.
If 'the badge' is not 0 and 'the compass' then, Print "ASSERT ENV-05: expected 0 got {'the compass'}", Exit 95. Print 'the badge' as a boolean.
If 'the badge' is 0 and 'the compass' is false then, Print "ASSERT ENV-02: expected 1 got {'the compass'}", Exit 95. Print 'the compass'.

    a number called 'the locale' is environment's count,
    If 'the locale' is not 0 and environment's empty then, Print "ASSERT ENV-05: expected 0 got {environment's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the locale' as a boolean,
    If 'the locale' is 0 and environment's empty is false then, Print "ASSERT ENV-02: expected 1 got {environment's empty}", Exit 95. Print environment's empty.

--- ENV-06 (ENV-03, ENV-04): a lookup read several ways agrees with itself ---
a text called 'the letterbox' is environment's first.
a buffer called 'the letterbox in bytes' is 'the letterbox'.
a buffer called 'the headcount' is environment's first.
If 'the headcount's size is not 'the letterbox in bytes''s size then, Print "ASSERT ENV-03: expected {'the letterbox in bytes''s size} got {'the headcount's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the headcount's size.
If 'the headcount's empty is not 'the letterbox in bytes''s empty then, Print "ASSERT ENV-03: expected {'the letterbox in bytes''s empty} got {'the headcount's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the headcount's empty.
Print 'the headcount's size.

    a text called 'the house number' is environment's "MAIL",
    a buffer called 'the house number in bytes' is 'the house number',
    a buffer called 'the badge' is environment's "MAIL",
    If 'the badge's size is not 'the house number in bytes''s size then, Print "ASSERT ENV-06: expected {'the house number in bytes''s size} got {'the badge's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the badge's size,
    If 'the badge's empty is not 'the house number in bytes''s empty then, Print "ASSERT ENV-06: expected {'the house number in bytes''s empty} got {'the badge's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the badge's empty,
    Print 'the badge's size.

a text called 'the locale' is environment's "VOXFUZZ_UNSET_351191".
a buffer called 'the locale in bytes' is 'the locale'.
a buffer called 'the doormat' is environment's "VOXFUZZ_UNSET_351191".
If 'the doormat's size is not 'the locale in bytes''s size then, Print "ASSERT ENV-06: expected {'the locale in bytes''s size} got {'the doormat's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the doormat's size.
If 'the doormat's empty is not 'the locale in bytes''s empty then, Print "ASSERT ENV-06: expected {'the locale in bytes''s empty} got {'the doormat's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the doormat's empty.
a buffer called 'the doorbell' is environment's "VOXFUZZ_UNSET_351191".
If 'the doorbell's size is not 'the locale in bytes''s size then, Print "ASSERT ENV-06: expected {'the locale in bytes''s size} got {'the doorbell's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the doorbell's size.
If 'the doorbell's empty is not 'the locale in bytes''s empty then, Print "ASSERT ENV-06: expected {'the locale in bytes''s empty} got {'the doorbell's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the doorbell's empty.
If the environment variable "VOXFUZZ_UNSET_351191" exists then, Print "ASSERT ENV-10: expected 0 got 1", Exit 95. Print 'the locale in bytes''s empty.
Print 'the doorbell's size.

--- ENV-10, ENV-11: the exists predicate ---
a boolean called 'the house number' is false.
If the environment variable "DISPLAY" exists then, Set 'the house number' to true. Print 'the house number'.
a text called 'the noticeboard' is "elsewhere".
If arguments's count is greater than 1 then, Set 'the noticeboard' to arguments's first. But if the environment variable "VOXFUZZ_UNSET_422516" exists then, Set 'the noticeboard' to environment's "VOXFUZZ_UNSET_422516". Print 'the noticeboard'.
Print 'the house number'.

    a boolean called 'the street sign' is false,
    If the environment variable "VOXFUZZ_UNSET_242642" exists then, Set 'the street sign' to true. Print 'the street sign',
    a boolean called 'the street sign seen again' is false,
    If the environment variable "VOXFUZZ_UNSET_242642" exists then, Set 'the street sign seen again' to true. Print 'the street sign seen again',
    If 'the street sign seen again' is not 'the street sign' then, Print "ASSERT ENV-10: expected {'the street sign'} got {'the street sign seen again'}", Exit 95. Print 'the street sign seen again',
    If 'the street sign' then, Print "ASSERT ENV-10: expected 0 got 1", Exit 95. Print 'the street sign'.

a boolean called 'the visitor book' is false.
If the environment variable "PWD" exists then, Set 'the visitor book' to true. Print 'the visitor book'.
a text called 'the signpost' is "present".
If arguments's count is greater than 1 then, Set 'the signpost' to arguments's first. But if the environment variable "VOXFUZZ_UNSET_902009" exists then, Set 'the signpost' to environment's "VOXFUZZ_UNSET_902009". Print 'the signpost'.
Print 'the visitor book'.

--- ENV-03, ENV-04: an entry contains an equals sign ---
a text called 'the badge' is environment's last.
a buffer called 'the badge in bytes' is 'the badge'.
a number called 'the badge equals signs' is 0.
For each mark from 1 to 'the badge in bytes''s size, If byte mark of 'the badge in bytes' is 61 then, Set 'the badge equals signs' to 'the badge equals signs' add 1..
If 'the badge in bytes''s size is not 0 and 'the badge equals signs' is 0 then, Print "ASSERT ENV-04: expected 1 got {'the badge equals signs'}", Exit 95. Print 'the badge equals signs' as a boolean.
a buffer called 'the doorbell' is environment's last.
If 'the doorbell's size is not 'the badge in bytes''s size then, Print "ASSERT ENV-04: expected {'the badge in bytes''s size} got {'the doorbell's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the doorbell's size.
Print 'the badge in bytes''s size as a boolean.

--- the dispatchers ---
a boolean called 'the letterbox' is environment's empty.
If environment's count is not 0 and 'the letterbox' then, Print "ASSERT ENV-05: expected 0 got {'the letterbox'}", Exit 95. Print environment's count as a boolean.
If environment's count is 0 and 'the letterbox' is false then, Print "ASSERT ENV-02: expected 1 got {'the letterbox'}", Exit 95. Print 'the letterbox'.

a text called 'the missing value 11' is environment's "VOXFUZZ_UNSET_643460".
On error print "environment variable not set".
Print 'the missing value 11'.

